# Secrets — never commit. .env.example and .env.j2 are TRACKED templates, so
# `.env.*` does not affect them (gitignore never applies to tracked files) —
# IaC-Stack's env-file.yml treats a missing template as success and the service
# would otherwise start with every ${VAR} interpolated empty.
#
# No `!` negations anywhere in this file: it has a second reader. IaC-Stack's
# rsync-build translates every line into an `--exclude`, and a leading `!` there
# does not un-exclude one pattern — it clears every rule collected above it, so
# the protection for data/, logs/ and .env would silently fall away. The role
# refuses the whole deploy rather than mistranslate it.
.env
.env.*

# Local cache / state
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
cache/
data/

# Build output
/git-planner
/dist/
/bin/

# Logs
logs/
*.log

# Editor / OS
# The impeccable design hook keeps its config here (committed — the two
# rule suppressions are reviewable decisions that belong to this repo) next to
# a per-run cache and a pending-findings file, which do not.
.impeccable/hook.cache.json
.impeccable/hook.pending.json
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/*

# Go
*.test
*.out
vendor/
